  `q` (`Thin<S>`, NCA5's `checkThin`); the partial sums `2..5` of the radix
  node (`Conv<S><n>`, `checkConv`); NCA1's `checkFinal` on the root-loss
  marginal with `p = qc / 2^(64-k+t)` (`Final<S>`). P10r's truncation term is
  at most `g · 10^-47` (NCA5's `eps_bound` at `c = 316`, `e = 47`). One target per shape (the larger class,
  rounded up to five significant digits) serves both classes.

